            <ArticleTitle>[Intraparietal hemorrhage of the small intestine related to hypocoagulation as an unusual cause of hemoperitoneum].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>249-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present a case of acute abdomen, spontaneous hemoperitoneum, caused by intraparietal hemorrhage of the small intestine in a patient with hypocoagulation that was pharmacologically induced by warfarin anticoagulation therapy. Potential etiology of the described case is considered by the authors.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
